    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1177
    pr_ref:  # 1177
    description: "Source: a second outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, made after the fixes from the first review merged. Each claim was re-checked against those files and the code on dev fed15705d7, then measured on 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo (default sketch and --no-source, 8k/32k/128k). Scripts, the 120 sketches and results.txt: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026.\n\nOBSERVED. The sketch Configuration section prints a cut-off TOML value as the licence:\n  packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml: name: hypergumbo; version: 9.2.0; license: { text =\neight times on the self-run (source line: license = { text = \"AGPL-3.0-or-later\" }), 14 times on kserve and once on mitmproxy; sqlalchemy prints \"version: {attr =\". That is 3 of the 6 other repositories whose sketch has a pyproject.toml line (httpx, poetry and pydantic-core print whole values).\n\nMECHANISM. sketch._extract_pyproject_toml reads name, version and license with the regular expression ^field\\s*=\\s*[\"']?([^\"'#\\n]+) over the file's text. It stops at the first quote, so an inline table ({ text = \"...\" }, { file = \"LICENSE\" }) is cut after its first key. It is not scoped to a table, so the first line starting with name or version anywhere in the file is taken, including [tool.*] tables and arrays of tables. It cannot read version = { attr = ... } or dynamic = [\"version\"]. The sibling readers in the same function family are also regular expressions over text (read in the code, not run): _extract_cargo_toml (misses version.workspace = true and license.workspace = true silently, and takes the first name = \"...\" in the file, which is a [[bin]] or [lib] name when that table comes first), and _extract_package_json prints a license object as a Python dict.\n\nASK. Read each manifest with its parser (tomllib or tomli for TOML, which the packages already depend on; json for package.json), take fields from the table that defines them, and render a structured value as its meaning (the licence text or file name, \"workspace\" for an inherited field). A field the reader cannot resolve is left out, never printed half-read. Acceptance: on a corpus, no Configuration line contains an unbalanced brace or quote.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was first seen. A fix keyed to this repository's paths or file names, or one that works for one language only, does not close this item.\nThe rule (parse the format; a value is printed whole or not at all) covers every manifest reader in sketch.py: package.json, go.mod, pom.xml, Cargo.toml, pyproject.toml, mix.exs, build.gradle, Gemfile. A fix to the pyproject reader alone does not close this item."  # 1177
    fields: {}  # 1177
